    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d27">

                <pb facs="0463" n="449" xml:id="pg449"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Monroe, Secretary of State, to Mr. Conner.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of
                        State</hi></placeName>,<lb/><date calendar="gregorian" when="1814-04-19"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">April</hi> 19, 1814</date>.</dateline>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The papers referred to in your letter of
                    the 7th instant were duly received at this office. The United States being at
                    peace with Spain, no countenance can be given by their Government to the
                    proceedings of the revolutionary party in East Florida, if it is composed of
                    Spanish subjects, and still less can it be given to them if it consists of
                    American citizens, who, so far as their conduct may fall within the scope of
                    existing laws long enacted and well known and understood, will be liable to
                    censure.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES MONROE.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson Conner</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Louisburgh, North Carolina.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
